## Decisions and Action Items

*   **Decision**: The Math in RFCs draft (`draft-editorial-rswg-mathinrfcs`) is approved as amended by Eliot Lear's text change ("may" instead of "is expected to"). The chairs will submit this completed document to the RSAB.
*   **Decision**: Mirja Kühlewind’s "updates" tag draft is officially put on hold (in abeyance) pending the outcomes of the Evolving RFCs discussion.
*   **Action Item**: Jean Mahoney (RPC) to draft an outline/list of existing RPC policies and conventions regarding author/editor handling (such as procedures for deceased, missing, or non-responsive authors) to help level-set the authorship discussion.
*   **Action Item**: Brian Carpenter to revise the authorship guidelines draft, reframing its core principles around "author responsibility" instead of tool/AI disclosure.
*   **Action Item**: The chairs to issue a mailing list poll to schedule an interim RSWG meeting to discuss the Evolving RFCs initiative.

